{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game","id":1004595,"title":"Wolf populations & where you set your game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T13:16:47-08:00","id":1004595,"title":"Wolf populations & where you set your game?","content":"Basically, do you take into consideration the real life presence/absence of wolf populations when choosing where your game is set?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:35:15-08:00","id":1004635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game#post1004595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, do you take into consideration the real life presence/absence of wolf populations when choosing where your game is set?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost never.<br /> The WoD is a different world, so I don't feel the need. The best example (imo) of the books doing this is the Hakken of Japan. They still have Wolf Kinfolk even through Japan hasn't had wolves on over a century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:50:45-08:00","id":1004649,"title":"","content":"I take it into consideration when determining the setting in the area I set my game in. However, I usually select the place where my game is set because there's something that prompts interest in it or inspires something that I like which I can use in Werewolf. I find most of my players actually are not interested in playing Lupus characters or wanting real wolves around them, so it's a moot point. If they did, it would probably influence where I set the game.<br /> <br /> I try to keep my chronicle mirroring the real world on a general basis, but don't have issues making adjustments in order to accommodate the needs of the game. Generally, the wolf population will be a bit more prevalent in the World of Darkness since the Garou will protect some small population where they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T19:57:36-08:00","id":1004768,"title":"","content":"I do and don't. In the real world the last recorded wolf pack in Pennsylvania was killed in Lancaster Co. in 1912 on land that is now an elementary school. Instead of this event I have moved the last wolf pack to a sanctuary created on an island in the Susquehanna river this is the home of a small Red Talon Sept. The Uktena have a small pack of kinfolk wolf hidden on the lands of the Sept of Rattlesnake's Wisdom(rattlesnakes are not found often in Lancaster Co. mostly Copperheads and those are really common) the Get of Fenris have established a wolf sanctuary for &quot;rescued&quot; wolves that houses more wolf kinfolk. It really isn't hard to figure out how to include wolves where they shouldn't be common sense can give you a reason. <br /> For stories I set outside of the Lanc. Co area I tend to wing it. My semi-planned Michigan chronicle for instance I have several large wolf packs in the area and have the Red Talons making small cautious moves to reclaiming a city by infiltrating Detroit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:02:17-08:00","id":1004771,"title":"","content":"I tend to go with real world population, with the addition of sufficient wolf populations for Kinfolk. There are probably ~2,000 Lupus, so I would have ~200,000 Wolf Kinfolk in addition to the ~200,000 mundane wolves. Wolf Kinfolk are hidden from the public by the actions of Human Kinfolk and the magic of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T03:33:03-08:00","id":1004862,"title":"","content":"Given this is my bread and butter, I do. I take note of the local subspecies, what it looks like and its habits.<br /> <br /> However, I do not consider populations as much. Given garou are around, especially lupus, wolf populations would be far more numerous than in our world. However, ironically I'm not sure if they would be as genetically varied. Since a lot of tribes base their pure breed on fur colour, some even breeding for very doggy pelts like the Black Furies, there would be a lot more selective breeding going on with the wolves than in our world.<br /> <br /> For example, black wolves are mostly an American thing and one that stems from wolfdogs as purely black coats are a dog trait. So, for Shadow Lords to uphold that type of colour, they need to have been very VERY critical on who to breed with. And given they are described as pitbull-like, I'd say it shows. Then there are Silver Fangs and their spread and white/silver coats. While white wolves do exist, they are limited to two subspecies at most. So Silver Fangs would have had to selectively crossbreed with local wolf populations to get white wolves to India or the Middle East.<br /> <br /> Of course, the people of WoD just see reddish, piebald, bi-colour and other wolf coats as normal wolf markings, since that is how things are in their world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:48:45-08:00","id":1004967,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the general consensus seems to be &quot;you can, but WoD wouldn't be the same due to Garou, so it's not a deal breaker&quot;. I can work with that. I'm looking at using Death Valley as the center point of my next game, but I'm 100% on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:55:28-08:00","id":1004969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game?p=1004967#post1004967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so the general consensus seems to be &quot;you can, but WoD wouldn't be the same due to Garou, so it's not a deal breaker&quot;. I can work with that. I'm looking at using Death Valley as the center point of my next game, but I'm 100% on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there supposed to be Black Spiral Dancers out that way? Manson Family was there, and if I remember he was rumored to be one of their kin... on the other hand I am not around my books and my memory is pretty much shot (don't do model glue, not even once).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:05:17-08:00","id":1005001,"title":"","content":"There is also a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubehebe_Crater\" target=\"_blank\">dormant volcano that it may only have been 800 years since it's last eruption</a>, so I plan on having there be a sleeping ancient spirit underneath that they'll have to worry about keeping asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:18:02-08:00","id":1005009,"title":"","content":"Hm, Death Valley is coyote country, not wolf country, and wolves would die due to the heat (now, if they are being kept as virtual pets by Human Kinfolk they might survive, but I think they would rather be 500 miles further north). There is no reason why a Garou pack cannot be down there though, as Moon Bridges and modern transportation make it a relatively short trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:34:48-08:00","id":1005019,"title":"","content":"I definitely plan to include Nuwisha, Mokole, and the occasional other Fera in the game. The heat will play a factor in the mood of the campaign too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:47:52-08:00","id":1005024,"title":"","content":"Coywolves, they do happen and depending on the tribes involved, might be accepted into the Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:06:34-08:00","id":1005096,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if they would. Is there anything in the books that say so one way or another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:14:48-08:00","id":1005099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game?p=1005096#post1005096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if they would. Is there anything in the books that say so one way or another?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't, granted. But it is sometimes look at what actual nature is like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:24:02-08:00","id":1005102,"title":"","content":"There was at least 2 threads relatively recently on coyote-wolf hybrids. Red wolves (which often have coyote DNA at this point) who go through the Change are Garou, so I don't see an issue with the concept. Too much coyote DNA though should lead to the Changer being Nuwisha (with that silly large Merit they had) instead of Garou imo.<br /> <br /> Either way, the books don't actually cover this so it's up to the ST to decide how to proceed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:02:08-08:00","id":1005188,"title":"","content":"Coyote-wolf hybrids do not occur in the desert though because it is not wolf territory (everywhere is coyote territory when humans kill off enough bears, cougars, and wolves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:14:12-08:00","id":1005224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game?p=1004635#post1004635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost never.<br /> The WoD is a different world, so I don't feel the need. The best example (imo) of the books doing this is the Hakken of Japan. They still have Wolf Kinfolk even through Japan hasn't had wolves on over a century.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> . IRL Wolves in Japan are officially extinct but are also a subject of cryptozoology, so to me it stands to reason in a world where there's actual supernatural creatures hidden that many mundane entities and conspiracies might slip through the cracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:49:27-08:00","id":1005238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game?p=1005224#post1005224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. IRL Wolves in Japan are officially extinct but are also a subject of cryptozoology, so to me it stands to reason in a world where there's actual supernatural creatures hidden that many mundane entities and conspiracies might slip through the cracks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. But that isn't an argument against not worrying about where real life wolf populations are in the WoD since they could likewise just be hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T00:26:16-08:00","id":1005267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1004595-wolf-populations-where-you-set-your-game?p=1005238#post1005238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that. But that isn't an argument against not worrying about where real life wolf populations are in the WoD since they could likewise just be hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't mean it as an argument against such examples but rather as a broad justification for the wolf population being larger in a world where myths are true, since there are modern myths of wolves suriving in Japan. Similarly other anomolous animals are good fodder for potential small lineages of forgotten Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:47:58-08:00","id":1006519,"title":"","content":"The games I run are usually set geographically close to where I live which, luckily enough, is in western states with established wolf populations. The Werewolf source books usually say that the Garou keep wolf packs around somewhere for breeding purposes. If I recall it causes a lot of issues for the Glass Walkers because it's disrespectful to keep wolf Kin in cages but you obviously can't keep them in a city either. Major contributing factor to their general lack of Lupus members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T08:32:07-08:00","id":1006723,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess I hadn't been considering that werewolves don't actually necessarily need there to be real wolf populations around. They can either keep their wolf kinfolk secret or just have human kinfolk. This has all been a huge help everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}